---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { meta, fmt } from '../lib/data';
const kz = meta.kaizoku as { dataset?: string; manifestDate?: string } | undefined;
const opb = meta.opbounty as { set?: string } | undefined;
const one = meta.optcgone as { fetchedAt?: string; rankedCount?: number } | undefined;
---
<Base title="About">
  <h1>About</h1>
  <div class="panel">
    <p>OPTCG Data is a free, unofficial view of the OPTCG Sim ranked ladder: the top players, their bounty, the leaders they play, and the decks and cards winning with those leaders.</p>
    <p>Nothing is fetched live. A scheduled job pulls each source <b>once a day</b>, merges it, and rebuilds this static site. Leader, matchup and decklist views default to the last 7 days; a 30-day view is built by summing one daily snapshot per day, so it fills in as days accumulate. Last updated: <b>{meta.date}</b> ({meta.generatedAt}).</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Data Sources</h2>
  <div class="panel">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Source</th><th>What we use</th><th>Snapshot</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><a href="https://stats.tcgmatchmaking.com/">OPBounty</a> <span class="muted">(TCG Match Making)</span></td><td>Standard ladder top 1,000: bounty, records, top leaders. Published ranked statistics: OPBounty's own complete aggregates of every ranked game (leaders, first/second splits, matchups and every distinct decklist with its record), which are the numbers on the Leaders, Matchups and leader pages. Replay archive: about half of ranked games with both decklists and combat logs, which supplies who piloted what and per-player game histories. Sim handles from combat logs for games above bounty 1,900. Player profiles: each player's own season record, top-3 leader stats with first/second splits, bounty after every game and their newest public matches with decklists, which are the season figures on player pages and the ladder.</td><td>set <code>{opb?.set}</code> · {String((meta as any).windows?.['30d']?.archiveDays ?? 0)} days archived</td><td>{meta.status.opbounty} / {meta.status.matches ?? 'n/a'}</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="https://www.cardkaizoku.com/">Card Kaizoku</a></td><td>1st/2nd turn split, per-card usage and win rate, tech cards, opening hands (weekly). Per-account decklists where a ladder name matches. Card database.</td><td><code>{kz?.dataset}</code> · {kz?.manifestDate}</td><td>{meta.status.kaizoku}</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="https://www.optcg.one/">optcg.one</a></td><td>Ranked decklists with region / Elo tier ({fmt(one?.rankedCount, 0)} lists).</td><td>{one?.fetchedAt?.slice(0, 10)}</td><td>{meta.status.optcgone}</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p style="font-size:.85rem">Both OPBounty and Card Kaizoku are one-person community projects funded through Patreon. If this site is useful to you, support them:
      <a href="https://www.patreon.com/tcgmm">TCG Match Making on Patreon</a> · <a href="https://www.patreon.com/cardkaizoku">Card Kaizoku on Patreon</a>.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>How Decks Are Merged</h2>
  <div class="panel" style="font-size:.9rem">
    <p>Each source publishes decklists in its own shape. We normalise every list to <code>quantity × card id</code>, drop the leader line, sort, and hash. Lists with the same hash are one deck. Games and win rate combine the ladder pool and the sim-wide pool; where two feeds describe the same pool we keep the larger sample rather than double counting.</p>
    <p>Per-player exact decklists are not published by any free source, so a player page shows the top-performing lists for the leaders that player pilots.</p>
    <p>"Copy for sim" puts the list on your clipboard in the format OPTCG Sim imports.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Privacy</h2>
  <div class="panel" style="font-size:.9rem">
    <p>We store only what is shown: display name, bounty, records, country and leader usage for players in the ladder top 1,000. Device identifiers and account handles present in upstream data are discarded at ingest. To have your name removed, <a href="https://github.com/alexfrey317/optcg-data/issues">open an issue on the repository</a>.</p>
    <p>Source code: <a href="https://github.com/alexfrey317/optcg-data">github.com/alexfrey317/optcg-data</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
